  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Crystalline solids are said to have a regular arrangement of atoms, ions or molecules. List three more characteristics of a crystalline solid. (3 marks)', 'Besides a regular, long-range ordered arrangement of particles, crystalline solids: (1) have a sharp and definite melting point; (2) are anisotropic - properties such as refractive index and electrical conductivity differ in different directions; (3) have a definite and characteristic heat of fusion; (4) have a definite geometric shape and break (cleave) along definite planes to give smooth, flat surfaces. They are called true solids (e.g. NaCl, quartz, diamond).', null, '[{"point": "Sharp, definite melting point", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Anisotropic - physical properties differ in different directions; definite geometric shape and long-range order", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Definite heat of fusion; cleave along planes giving smooth surfaces; true solids", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
