  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Benzene is the simplest and most important aromatic hydrocarbon.
(a) Name the scientist who discovered it, the year of discovery, and the material in which it was first discovered. (1.5 marks)
(b) Give the reason why it is named benzene. What is its formula and its commercial name? (1.5 marks)', '(a) Benzene was discovered by Michael Faraday in 1825; he isolated it from the oily liquid that condensed from compressed illuminating gas (made from whale oil/ coal gas), calling it ''bicarburet of hydrogen''. (b) It is named after gum benzoin: in 1834 Eilhard Mitscherlich obtained it by heating benzoic acid (from gum benzoin) with lime and called it ''benzin'', which became benzene. Its molecular formula is C6H6, and its commercial name is benzol.', null, '[{"point": "(a) Michael Faraday, 1825, in the oily residue (compressed illuminating gas) from whale/ coal gas", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "(b) Named from gum benzoin/ benzoic acid (Mitscherlich obtained it from benzoic acid - ''benzin''); formula C6H6; commercial name benzol", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'bio-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
