  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'In thermodynamics, a system is a specific portion of matter under study, separated from the rest of the universe by a boundary. Name the different types of systems and briefly explain them with an example. (3 marks)', '(1) Open system - can exchange both matter and energy with its surroundings; e.g. water being heated in an open beaker (vapour escapes and heat enters), or a living cell. (2) Closed system - can exchange energy but not matter; e.g. water heated in a sealed metal container. (3) Isolated system - can exchange neither matter nor energy; e.g. hot tea in an ideal (perfectly insulated) thermos flask.', null, '[{"point": "Open system: exchanges both matter and energy with the surroundings, e.g. water boiling in an open beaker, living organisms", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Closed system: exchanges energy but not matter, e.g. water in a closed (sealed) vessel being heated", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Isolated system: exchanges neither matter nor energy, e.g. hot tea in an ideal thermos flask", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
